    "body": "pulse task #2904 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:83627035472be5d92ab353eca1e7df72 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2904: Sampler MVP: wire the basic sample controls into a clean panel\n\nOperation: 83627035472be5d92ab353eca1e7df72\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nTarget: one stable, usable native Sampler panel with actual sample identification/waveform and supported pitch, gain, start/end, loop and amplitude-envelope controls. Acceptance: visible controls read actual retained device values and send canonical edits; bounds remain valid, audio/preview reflects accepted values, pending/stale/refused edits remain truthful, and selection/A-B/device changes cannot edit a different instance. Use shared widgets/current theme and compact layout; no placeholder controls, owning-state cache under scoped reads or old EQ automation resurrection. Demonstrate load then each basic control and supported compact sizing; targeted real UI/input/read-failure regressions.\n\nOwner: sole existing Local UI writer; Native provides only genuinely missing typed contracts, merger preserves Main/current behavior. Functional dependency sample load for complete demonstration; panel/read/command wiring proceeds independently now. Advanced modes/filter/LFO/modulation/warp remain deferred parent2679.\n\nSplit from #2789/canonical PR395, Playable Sampler MVP goal5. Preserve existing implementation/WIP there. Canonical intake draft is a tracking shell until deliberate focused source handoff; no copying edits into a competing implementation or automatic task start. Completion requires this target's actual acceptance, not split/draft/parent merge alone.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
